1.7 2-3.5 2-5.2 0-1.7-2-3.5-2-5.2 0-1.7 2-3.5 2-5.2 0-1.7-2-3.5-2-5.2 0-1.7 2-3.5 2-5.2 0"></path></svg><div class="_1b0azjk7"><div class="_126fmnp7 _126fmnp0"><div class="_126fmnpb _126fmnp9 _126fmnpi"><div class="duet--article--article-byline e8ciraa mizka60"><span class=""><span>by</span> <!-- --> <span class="mizka62 mizka63"><a href="https://www.eater.com/authors/shindy-chen">Shindy Chen</a></span> and <!-- --> <span class="mizka62 mizka63"><a href="https://www.eater.com/authors/kayleigh-ruller">Kayleigh Ruller</a></span></span></div><span class="duet--article--timestamp _1fefrso6 _1fefrso1 _1fefrso0 e8cira5 e8ciraa">Updated <time dateTime="2026-02-02T19:21:58+00:00">Feb 2, 2026, 7:21 PM UTC</time></span></div><div class="_126fmnp1s _126fmnp1y"><div class="_126fmnp1p _126fmnp1h"><div class="uqiuaba uqiuab8 uqiuab0 uqiuab2i"><div class="uqiuab0 uqiuabb uqiuab9" data-concert="article_sponsorship_desktop"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="_1b0azjk5"><div><span class="_126fmnp17"><ul class="duet--article--share-buttons _10aacrv0"><li><button aria-label="Share on Facebook" class="_10aacrv2 _10aacrv1"><svg class="_10aacrvd _10aacrvc" width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><title>Facebook</title><path d="M27.0174 21.7497L27.8495 16.3604H22.6403V12.8637C22.6403 11.3906 23.3668 9.95151 25.7019 9.95151H28.0714V5.36435C28.0714 5.36435 25.9212 5 23.866 5C19.5761 5 16.7707 7.57929 16.7707 12.2529V16.3604H12V21.7497H16.7707V34.7746C17.727 34.924 18.707 35 19.7055 35C20.704 35 21.6841 34.9214 22.6403 34.7746V21.7497H27.0174Z" fill=""></path></svg></button></li><li><div class="_10aacrvo"><button aria-label="Copy link" class="_10aacrv2 _10aacrv1"><svg class="_10aacrvd _10aacrvc" width="40" height="40" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 40 40" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><title>Link</title><path d="M16.9691 32.9499C14.2358 35.6832 9.78321 35.6832 7.04996 32.9499C4.31671 30.2166 4.31665 25.764 7.04996 23.0307L12.5606 17.52C15.294 14.7867 19.7465 14.7867 22.4798 17.52C22.704 17.7383 22.8315 18.037 22.8337 18.3499C22.8359 18.6628 22.7125 18.9634 22.4912 19.1846C22.2702 19.4059 21.9693 19.5293 21.6568 19.5271C21.3439 19.5249 21.0449 19.3975 20.8266 19.1732C18.9805 17.3271 16.0599 17.3271 14.2137 19.1732L8.70306 24.6839C6.85694 26.53 6.85694 29.4507 8.70306 31.2968C10.5492 33.1429 13.4698 33.1426 15.3159 31.2968L20.551 26.0614V26.0617C20.7693 25.8375 21.0683 25.71 21.3811 25.7078C21.694 25.7056 21.9946 25.829 22.2159 26.0503C22.4368 26.2716 22.5602 26.5722 22.5581 26.885C22.5559 27.1979 22.4284 27.4966 22.2042 27.7149L16.9691 32.9499ZM27.4394 22.4796C24.706 25.2129 20.2535 25.2129 17.5202 22.4796V22.4799C17.296 22.2616 17.1685 21.9629 17.1663 21.65C17.1644 21.3372 17.2875 21.0366 17.5088 20.8153C17.7301 20.5941 18.0307 20.4707 18.3435 20.4728C18.6564 20.475 18.9551 20.6025 19.1734 20.8267C21.0195 22.6728 23.9401 22.6728 25.7863 20.8267L31.2969 15.316C33.1431 13.4699 33.1431 10.5493 31.2969 8.70316C29.4508 6.85704 26.5302 6.85704 24.6841 8.70316L19.449 13.9382C19.2307 14.1625 18.9317 14.2902 18.6189 14.2924C18.306 14.2946 18.0054 14.1712 17.7841 13.9499C17.5629 13.7286 17.4395 13.428 17.4417 13.1149C17.4438 12.802 17.5713 12.503 17.7958 12.285L23.0309 7.04999C25.7642 4.31667 30.2168 4.31667 32.95 7.04999C35.6833 9.7833 35.6834 14.2359 32.95 16.9691L27.4394 22.4798L27.4394 22.4796Z"></path></svg></button></div></li></ul></span></div><span class="ocstib1"><button type="button" class="ocstib0" aria-label="Save this guide"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="2 2 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.2002 20.3202L12.4176 15.0407L17.6349 20.3202V8.24064C17.6349 5.67699 15.43 3.6001 12.7113 3.6001H7.2002V20.3202Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div><div class="duet--article--article-body-component"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 va4xi86 va4xi85 e8cira1">More often than not, tipsters, readers, friends, and family of Eater ask: Where should I eat right now? What’s new? Have you been yet? While the <a href="/maps/best-restaurants-charlotte-north-carolina">Eater 18</a> covers the Queen City’s old standbys and essentials, it is not a chronicle of the “it” places of the moment. Enter this Eater Heatmap, which highlights new spots under a year old and has crowds flocking and people talking. Try one of these today.</p></div><div class="duet--article--article-body-component"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 e8cira1"><em>New to the list: Seaboy, Emmy Lou’s, DŌZO, Prime Fish Cellar, and the Story of Mi Cariño. Locations are listed geographically from north to south.</em></p></div></div><div class=""><div><div class="duet--article--map-card hkfm3h0" data-slug="seaboy" id="seaboy"><div class="hkfm3h2"></div><div class="hkfm3h3"><h2 class="hkfm3h5">Seaboy</h2><span class="hkfm3h6"><button type="button" class="_6ylzph0" aria-label="Save to a list"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="2 2 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.2002 20.3202L12.4176 15.0407L17.6349 20.3202V8.24064C17.6349 5.67699 15.43 3.6001 12.7113 3.6001H7.2002V20.3202Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></button></span></div><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 e8cira1 hkfm3h9">Open since March 2025, Seaboy is chef Jonny Cox’s first solo endeavor as a chef and owner, and has Charlotteans driving north to the Lake Norman area to sample his seafood menu. This, especially after appearing on <a href="https://www.esquire.com/food-drink/restaurants/a69501755/best-new-restaurants-america-2025/">Esquire Magazine</a>’s list for 33 “Best New Restaurants in America.” Inside the standalone cottage, the decor is whimsical: think coastal grandma meets modern roadside shack, with a 10-table back dining room, and a lively front bar area which seats 12, including four chef’s counter seats and nine more patio tables coming in warmer months, and all offering the full menu. For the table, start with daily oysters with homemade hot sauce and mignonettes, the generous yellowfin crudo with bright benne seeds, and perfectly round, piping hot crab and chorizo croquettes. Follow with a beautifully plated, soul-warming sablefish or a surprising, lamb pappardelle ragu, which is homey and hearty.</p><div class="iyvbja0"><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.2226 0.779264C10.1836 -0.259755 8.49832 -0.259755 7.4593 0.779264L6.00095 2.23761L4.5426 0.779264C3.50359 -0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 0.779264 0.779264C-0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 3.50359 0.779264 4.5426L6.00007 9.76341L11.2209 4.5426C12.2599 3.50359 12.2599 1.81828 11.2209 0.779264H11.2226Z"></path></svg>Loved it</button><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.9998 1.90244L10.0973 0L3.91706 6.17935L1.90244 4.16474L0 6.06808L3.91706 9.98514L11.9998 1.90244Z"></path></svg>Want to try</button></div><ul class="hkfm3hb"><li class="hkfm3hc"><div class="_1motwwz0"><a class="_1motwwz1" href="https://reservations.safegraph.com/reserve/235298?utm_source=safegraph&amp;utm_campaign=poi" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer nofollow"><svg class="_1motwwz2" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><title>Booking</title><path fill="currentColor" d="M12.85,2.19c.39,0,.7.31.7.7v.72h1.43c1.17,0,2.12.95,2.12,2.12v9.96c0,1.17-.95,2.12-2.12,2.12H5.02c-1.17,0-2.12-.95-2.12-2.12V5.73c0-