9241_n.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0.01220703125%2C0%2C99.9755859375%2C100&amp;w=1440 1440w, https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/08/476484200_122096315558767110_2258668612190239241_n.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0.01220703125%2C0%2C99.9755859375%2C100&amp;w=1920 1920w, https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/08/476484200_122096315558767110_2258668612190239241_n.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0.01220703125%2C0%2C99.9755859375%2C100&amp;w=2048 2048w, https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/08/476484200_122096315558767110_2258668612190239241_n.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0.01220703125%2C0%2C99.9755859375%2C100&amp;w=2400 2400w" src="https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/08/476484200_122096315558767110_2258668612190239241_n.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0.01220703125%2C0%2C99.9755859375%2C100&amp;w=2400"/></div></div><div class="duet--media--caption _1l5wi2a1 _1l5wi2a0"><cite class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup e8cira2 _1l5wi2a6 _1l5wi2a5">Vavela Cafe</cite></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="duet--article--map-card hkfm3h0" data-slug="mchales-pub" id="mchales-pub"><div class="hkfm3h2"></div><div class="hkfm3h3"><h2 class="hkfm3h5">McHale’s Pub</h2><span class="hkfm3h6"><button type="button" class="_6ylzph0" aria-label="Save to a list"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="2 2 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.2002 20.3202L12.4176 15.0407L17.6349 20.3202V8.24064C17.6349 5.67699 15.43 3.6001 12.7113 3.6001H7.2002V20.3202Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></button></span></div><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 e8cira1 hkfm3h9">Apparently, Charlotte needed another bar — not a brewery, or a sceney cocktail joint, but an Irish pub. McHale’s, once in Fort Mill and Rock Hill, snagged the coveted space on North Davidson, and locals are flocking to it for the quaint snugs and the bona fide bar with Smithwicks, Guinness, and Harp. The outdoor beer garden fills up quickly, so go early and get the corned beef hash, ample fish and chips, Irish curry, or classic Irish breakfast.</p><div class="iyvbja0"><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.2226 0.779264C10.1836 -0.259755 8.49832 -0.259755 7.4593 0.779264L6.00095 2.23761L4.5426 0.779264C3.50359 -0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 0.779264 0.779264C-0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 3.50359 0.779264 4.5426L6.00007 9.76341L11.2209 4.5426C12.2599 3.50359 12.2599 1.81828 11.2209 0.779264H11.2226Z"></path></svg>Loved it</button><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.9998 1.90244L10.0973 0L3.91706 6.17935L1.90244 4.16474L0 6.06808L3.91706 9.98514L11.9998 1.90244Z"></path></svg>Want to try</button></div><ul class="hkfm3hb"><li class="hkfm3hd hkfm3hc"><a class="_1win6by0" target="_blank" href="https://lyft.sng.link/Ednq0/5pb9?_dl=lyft%3A%2F%2Fbook-a-ride%3Fdestination%5Baddress%5D%3D3112+North+Davidson+Street%2C+Charlotte%2C+North+Carolina+28205%2C+United+States&amp;utm_source=eater&amp;utm_medium=eaterapp&amp;utm_campaign=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination&amp;utm_term=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination&amp;utm_content=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination_Static&amp;_smtype=3" rel="noreferrer nofollow"><img class="_1win6by1" src="/static-assets/icons/lyft.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="17" height="12"/>Get there with Lyft<svg class="_1win6by2" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 1