-1.077.79-1.56 1.056-1.56Zm2.597 4.333h3.164a5.983 5.983 0 0 1 0 3.329h-3.164a19.528 19.528 0 0 0 0-3.33Zm2.772-1.004H12.49c-.179-1.23-.485-2.335-.914-3.12a6.023 6.023 0 0 1 3.801 3.12ZM8.44 5.212c-.43.785-.736 1.89-.914 3.12H4.638a6.023 6.023 0 0 1 3.802-3.12Zm-3.802 8.456h2.888c.178 1.23.484 2.335.914 3.12a6.023 6.023 0 0 1-3.802-3.12Zm6.938 3.12c.43-.785.735-1.89.914-3.12h2.887a6.023 6.023 0 0 1-3.801 3.12Z"></path></svg>Visit Website</a></li></ul><div class="hkfm3ha"><div class="_14k72og0"><div class="_14k72og2 _14k72og1 sticky-nav-trigger"></div><div class="_1fao6gze"></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="duet--article--map-card hkfm3h0" data-slug="eso-artisanal-pasta" id="eso-artisanal-pasta"><div class="hkfm3h2"></div><div class="hkfm3h3"><h2 class="hkfm3h5">Eso Artisanal Pasta</h2><span class="hkfm3h6"><button type="button" class="_6ylzph0" aria-label="Save to a list"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="2 2 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.2002 20.3202L12.4176 15.0407L17.6349 20.3202V8.24064C17.6349 5.67699 15.43 3.6001 12.7113 3.6001H7.2002V20.3202Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></button></span></div><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 e8cira1 hkfm3h9">The queues at Optimist Hall don’t lie; this pasta shop is special. Not just because everything is seasoned beautifully with long and slow, hearty, simmering flavors that would make any Italian nonna proud, but it’s the handmade pasta that captures the perfect balance of soft, chewy, and al dente. Husband and wife chef duo AJ and Kristina Sankofa brought their operation to Charlotte from New Jersey in early August, and since then, word of mouth is selling out even limited-time pasta specials like a $30 tajarin al tartufo to celebrate white truffle season. Though everything is decidedly tasty, a solid primer would be the hearty trottole ragu Napoletana, spicy Sicilian fried chicken (think General Tso’s chicken, but their version), just-creamy-enough bucatini cacio e pepe, and gnocchi ragu Napoletana.</p><div class="iyvbja0"><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.2226 0.779264C10.1836 -0.259755 8.49832 -0.259755 7.4593 0.779264L6.00095 2.23761L4.5426 0.779264C3.50359 -0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 0.779264 0.779264C-0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 3.50359 0.779264 4.5426L6.00007 9.76341L11.2209 4.5426C12.2599 3.50359 12.2599 1.81828 11.2209 0.779264H11.2226Z"></path></svg>Loved it</button><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.9998 1.90244L10.0973 0L3.91706 6.17935L1.90244 4.16474L0 6.06808L3.91706 9.98514L11.9998 1.90244Z"></path></svg>Want to try</button></div><ul class="hkfm3hb"><li class="hkfm3hd hkfm3hc"><a class="_1win6by0" target="_blank" href="https://lyft.sng.link/Ednq0/5pb9?_dl=lyft%3A%2F%2Fbook-a-ride%3Fdestination%5Baddress%5D%3D1115+North+Brevard+Street%2C+STE+D%2C+Charlotte%2C+North+Carolina+28206%2C+United+States&amp;utm_source=eater&amp;utm_medium=eaterapp&amp;utm_campaign=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination&amp;utm_term=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination&amp;utm_content=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination_Static&amp;_smtype=3" rel="noreferrer nofollow"><img class="_1win6by1" src="/static-assets/icons/lyft.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="17" height="12"/>Get there with Lyft<svg class="_1win6by2" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M8.85017 5.58349L5.68241 2.38336L6.25987 1.79