jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=2.8852152214598%2C0%2C94.22956955708%2C100&amp;w=1440 1440w, https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/11/Spaghette.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=2.8852152214598%2C0%2C94.22956955708%2C100&amp;w=1920 1920w, https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/11/Spaghette.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=2.8852152214598%2C0%2C94.22956955708%2C100&amp;w=2048 2048w, https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/11/Spaghette.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=2.8852152214598%2C0%2C94.22956955708%2C100&amp;w=2400 2400w" src="https://platform.carolinas.eater.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2025/11/Spaghette.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=2.8852152214598%2C0%2C94.22956955708%2C100&amp;w=2400"/></div><div class=""><div class="f607nx6"><div><div><div class=""></div><div><div class="e8cira9 _37drs88 _37drs80"><a class="_19vudfi0 _19vudfi4 _19vudfi5" href="/dining-report/45405/charlotte-spaghett-review">Charlotte’s Spaghett Offers Italian Comfort in a Quaint Historic Home</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="duet--article--map-card hkfm3h0" data-slug="painted-rooster" id="painted-rooster"><div class="hkfm3h2"></div><div class="hkfm3h3"><h2 class="hkfm3h5">Painted Rooster</h2><span class="hkfm3h6"><button type="button" class="_6ylzph0" aria-label="Save to a list"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="2 2 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.2002 20.3202L12.4176 15.0407L17.6349 20.3202V8.24064C17.6349 5.67699 15.43 3.6001 12.7113 3.6001H7.2002V20.3202Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></button></span></div><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 e8cira1 hkfm3h9">A new addition from Moo &amp; Brew owners in Plaza Midwood, and snugly situated across from Snug Harbor (though you can’t miss artist Matt Moore’s massive rainbow-colored rooster out front), the Painted Rooster’s go-to items are its crisped, flame-charred wings and Southern comfort foods that pair with an ample but unpretentious beer menu. Go for the Rooster signature wings or choose from more than 15 sauces (like honey lime Sriracha, Cheerwine barbecue, or ginger garlic soy) or six dry rubs (like lemon pepper or Moroccan), or a “Handheld Hootenanny BBQ” or Buffalo chicken wrap, one of many mac ‘n’ cheese options, or build your own salad.</p><div class="iyvbja0"><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.2226 0.779264C10.1836 -0.259755 8.49832 -0.259755 7.4593 0.779264L6.00095 2.23761L4.5426 0.779264C3.50359 -0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 0.779264 0.779264C-0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 3.50359 0.779264 4.5426L6.00007 9.76341L11.2209 4.5426C12.2599 3.50359 12.2599 1.81828 11.2209 0.779264H11.2226Z"></path></svg>Loved it</button><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.9998 1.90244L10.0973 0L3.91706 6.17935L1.90244 4.16474L0 6.06808L3.91706 9.98514L11.9998 1.90244Z"></path></svg>Want to try</button></div><ul class="hkfm3hb"><li class="hkfm3hd hkfm3hc"><a class="_1win6by0" target="_blank" href="https://lyft.sng.link/Ednq0/5pb9?_dl=lyft%3A%2F%2Fbook-a-ride%3Fdestination%5Baddress%5D%3D1601+Central+Avenue%2C+Charlotte%2C+North+Carolina+28205%2C+United+States&amp;utm_source=eater&amp;utm_medium=eaterapp&amp;utm_campaign=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination&amp;utm_term=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination&amp;utm_content=CheckLyft2026_Eater_Awareness_CLT_VenueDestination_Static&amp;_smtype=3" rel="noreferrer nofo