class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup e8cira2 _1l5wi2a6 _1l5wi2a5">Kudzu Bakery</cite></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="duet--article--map-card hkfm3h0" data-slug="sora" id="sora"><div class="hkfm3h2"></div><div class="hkfm3h3"><h2 class="hkfm3h5">Sora</h2><span class="hkfm3h6"><button type="button" class="_6ylzph0" aria-label="Save to a list"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="2 2 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.2002 20.3202L12.4176 15.0407L17.6349 20.3202V8.24064C17.6349 5.67699 15.43 3.6001 12.7113 3.6001H7.2002V20.3202Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"></path></svg></button></span></div><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph u67w0ti va4xi81 va4xi80 e8cira1 hkfm3h9">Sora is an exclusive French Asian fine dining affair from Charlotte restaurateur Birdie Yang of Yama and Baku. Appealing to the affluent neighborhood of Myers Park and those in search of hybrid fine dining and omakase concepts, this tasting menu highlights seafood-forward delicacies at $225 a person for chef’s counter seating and dining tables. A short-form tasting menu of four to five courses is also available at $125, as well as special omakase events with guest chefs.</p><div class="iyvbja0"><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill="currentColor" d="M11.2226 0.779264C10.1836 -0.259755 8.49832 -0.259755 7.4593 0.779264L6.00095 2.23761L4.5426 0.779264C3.50359 -0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 0.779264 0.779264C-0.259755 1.81828 -0.259755 3.50359 0.779264 4.5426L6.00007 9.76341L11.2209 4.5426C12.2599 3.50359 12.2599 1.81828 11.2209 0.779264H11.2226Z"></path></svg>Loved it</button><button type="button" class="iyvbja1" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="12" height="10" viewBox="0 0 12 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" x